# X-22 supporting evidence: where the N-bit covariance's registers go.
#
# Produced by scripts/covariance_nbit_codegen.sh on the reference device. It tests
# the obvious explanation for the ONE place the measured curve sits ABOVE the
# 3N^2+N model -- N = 4 with uint64_t words, 15.5x against a predicted 13.0x --
# namely register pressure, and REJECTS it: stack traffic and instruction count are
# within 2% of the uint32_t instantiation at every N, and the uint32_t N = 4 arm
# sits BELOW the model.
covariance N-bit codegen: stack traffic inside the kernel
  arch: aarch64   compiler: g++ (Debian 14.2.0-19) 14.2.0

  word       N         insns stack ld/st      bytes
  uint32_t   1           230         20        920
  uint32_t   2           382         60        860
  uint32_t   3           392         69        912
  uint32_t   4           399         69        948
  uint64_t   1           211         15        844
  uint64_t   2           382         60        856
  uint64_t   3           396         69        912
  uint64_t   4           406         70        944

  "stack ld/st" counts every load/store through sp or x29, prologue and
  epilogue included, so the number to read is its GROWTH with N rather than
  its absolute value.

# Environment: pi4, Raspberry Pi 4 Model B Rev 1.5, aarch64 / 6.18.34+rpt-rpi-v8,
# g++ (Debian 14.2.0-19) 14.2.0, performance governor, taskset -c 3,
# throttled=0x0 before and after.
